{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>וַיֵּצֵא לִקְרָאתוֹ אֶל עִיר מוֹאָב.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to specify the place from which he went out to meet him. It appears that the verse comes to relate Balaam's lowliness in Balak's eyes, for even though he heard of his arrival he did not go out to receive him in the manner of receiving great personages, who go out beyond the province; rather, only within the city itself. And this is its saying <b>וַיֵּצֵא לִקְרָאתוֹ אֶל עִיר מוֹאָב אֲשֶׁר עַל גְּבוּל</b> etc." "And its saying <b>בִּקְצֵה הַגְּבוּל</b> — perhaps it also intends to say that even this meager outing was not in his honor but for a reason, as they of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 20:16), and this is their language: What did Balak see to go out to meet him at the borders? He said to him: These borders were fixed from the days of Noah, that no nation should enter the territory of its fellow, and he would show him how [Sihon and Og] broke through and crossed the borders of Sihon and Og, up to here. And absent this reason he would not have gone out from his place."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:59.929280199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}